Field guidance:
- historical_evidence and failed_approaches: only records returned by a tool, with the status as recorded; empty lists
  if nothing relevant was returned.
- testability.p_testable: probability that the question can be answered with the stated data at useful statistical power.
- prior_work.already_answered: whether retrieved earlier work already answered substantially the same question.
  Use "unknown" if no earlier work was retrieved. List identifiers you relied on in prior_work.cited.
- predicted_outcome: probabilities (summing to 1) of what a competent test of the question as posed would conclude:
  supported, rejected (adequately powered null), untestable (cannot be tested with this data), artifact (apparent
  effect produced by a flaw), uncertain (inconclusive or inadequately tested).
- decision: proceed, proceed_with_changes (state the changes in design), or do_not_proceed.
- design: a pre-registration-quality plan even if the decision is do_not_proceed (then describe the minimum viable test).

{
 "research_concepts": [
  "lineup coverage of structural roles (organizer, shaper, terminal)",
  "within-team variation in lineup role coverage",
  "separability of role coverage from talent and player counts",
  "talent control in lineup-level influence measures"
 ],
 "methodological_questions": [
  "Is lineup role coverage separable from talent and roster counts once talent is controlled?",
  "Does talent control behave (no residual collinearity or over-adjustment) when coverage is measured per lineup within team?",
  "What sample size and exposure are needed for stable within-team lineup coverage estimates across 90 team-seasons?"
 ],
 "historical_evidence": [
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF18",
   "status_as_recorded": "supported",
   "finding": "Fragility confirmatory test. Structural influence was reported as not reducible to usage (F1a residual-share about 0.90 to 0.93, CIs excluding low values). Split-half residual influence was reported as reproducible (F1b pooled-residual rho about +0.67 to +0.69). Record notes limited measurement reliability (LIM:low_measurement_reliability; RISK:MEASURE_RELIABILITY)."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF17",
   "status_as_recorded": "supported",
   "finding": "Wiring confirmatory test. Team offensive association structure was reported as persistent across split halves (Frobenius S about 0.35) and as retaining similarity after residualising play-type rates (residual R2 about 0.043). This concerns team-level association structure, not lineup role coverage."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF20",
   "status_as_recorded": "untestable",
   "finding": "Absence validation. Gate G2 passed (21/23 above null median) and V1(a) passed (16/23 above own-null p95, binomial p=2.67e-16). The V2 prediction of absence-effect magnitude failed (V2a rho +0.288, p=0.077, CI spanning zero). Record notes LIM:small_sample."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPA-017",
   "status_as_recorded": "rejected",
   "finding": "Player-routing test. The A5 vs A3 signal fell from +0.94 pts/100 (V5) to +0.03 pts/100 on a 520-matchup sample (V6). The record classifies it as an adequately powered null (B_powered_null). Effects in this family shrank as sample size grew."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPA-066",
   "status_as_recorded": "not a hypothesis test",
   "finding": "TOV_FORCE matchup decomposition on four playoff games. Player-channel lifts were large on small cells (e.g. n_def 15 to 28), while team-level lifts were small. Record classifies the question as A_unanswerable with LIM:insufficient_exposure and RISK:EXPOSURE_SPARSITY."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-CHT-009",
   "status_as_recorded": "not a hypothesis test",
   "finding": "Superstar suppression by lineup and forced play type. Lineup-cell PPP gaps were reported for named stars (cells n about 30 to 59). The record states no placebo or matching was done and that later sequence work treated similar star-chain gaps as artifacts. Mechanism recorded as E_unclear."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPA-050",
   "status_as_recorded": "not a hypothesis test",
   "finding": "Sequential suppression by the preceding opponent play. A PUTBACK effect was reported for several stars, with n_after as low as 30 to 32 in some cells. The record states there was no multiplicity correction and that some cells were small against thousands of baseline possessions."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPM-022",
   "status_as_recorded": "inconclusive",
   "finding": "Superstar suppression profiles. The Q5c verdict was that the rank-1 suppressor varies across players, but most rank-1 deltas were within 1 to 2 SE with no multiple-comparison control. Verdict recorded as inconclusive."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPM-054",
   "status_as_recorded": "rejected",
   "finding": "Playoff adaptation-pair sustainability (74 matchups). Pairs with enough signal were recorded as PIVOT_LOSES, and most population deltas were under 0.10. Record classifies the outcome as an adequately powered null (B_powered_null) with LIM:small_sample."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-059",
   "status_as_recorded": "supported",
   "finding": "Sequence-memory horizon test on 1,024,980 possessions with a 2025-26 time-split. Short-memory horizon of about 2 to 3 possessions was supported, with most gain at lag 1 and absolute AUC about 0.591. This is a possession-level outcome study, not a coverage test."
